TWO THINGS TO READ OFF THIS TABLE BEFORE ANYTHING IS RUN:
  * the model's SURFACE DIC is right. 1986.3 against an observed 2028.9
    that carries ~50 umol/kg of anthropogenic carbon. The whole deficit is
    in the interior -- see this file's header on the dead hypothesis.
  * the DIC gradient is a THERMOCLINE feature, not an abyssal one: by
    923-1314 m the observations are already within ~8 umol/kg of the
    bottom. A pump that only fills the abyss would not reproduce it.
  * the observed SURFACE D14C is +52 permil, which is BOMB-CONTAMINATED
    and is NOT a preindustrial target. The model's -51 is not a misfit.
    Only the DEEP D14C row is used as a target, as it already is.


