TOTAL         21.99

literature global POC export at ~100 m: 5-12 GtC/yr
implied / literature midpoint:          2.6x

WHAT THIS NUMBER MEANS, AND IT IS A STRUCTURAL FINDING IN ITS OWN RIGHT.
The export required is set by how fast the model's diffusion DESTROYS the
gradient, i.e. by kz. A one-dimensional column has to use an EFFECTIVE kz
that stands in for three-dimensional advective ventilation, and 5000 m2/yr
is 9x Ledwell's NATRE thermocline diapycnal diffusivity, (1.7 +/- 0.2)e-5
m2/s = 536 m2/yr -- the repo's own sourced figure (redteam 2026-08-13 sec.1).
An effective diffusivity tuned to emulate TRANSPORT also spuriously
destroys GRADIENTS -- so in this model a pump must work several times
harder than the real one does. Read the ratio above with that in mind:
if it is well above 1, the gradient is telling us something about kz and
the column structure, not only about the missing biology.

NOTE: some boxes need a NEGATIVE source, i.e. removal at depth. That is
 not interpretable as remineralisation. It comes from the observed
 profile's slight mid-depth maximum (1314-1861 m is ~3 umol/kg above the
 bottom). Reported, not smoothed away; the magnitudes are printed above.

