=== PART 5. CAN ONE SOFT-TISSUE PUMP FIT BOTH OBSERVED GRADIENTS AT ONCE? ===
observed  dDIC +244.7 umol/kg,  d(d13C) -0.938 permil
all-organic prediction at eps = -20 permil: d(d13C) = -2.153 permil
i.e. a pure soft-tissue pump matching the DIC gradient overshoots
d13C by 2.3x.  Arm N measured 2.3x -- the two agree, so the
overshoot is ARITHMETIC and no choice of a single epsilon removes it.

two-component split implied by the observations (CaCO3 at +2.0 permil):
   soft-tissue  +111.0 umol/kg   (45 %)
   carbonate    +133.7 umol/kg   (55 %)

CONSEQUENCE FOR THE DESIGN. A pump that fits the DIC gradient AND the
d13C gradient needs TWO components, not one -- and the carbonate limb
also moves alkalinity, which this model holds FIXED at ALK_SURFACE. That
is a second structural commitment hiding behind the first. It is a
scoping fact for handoff 15c sec.5's design sign-off, not a defect here.
CAVEAT, stated rather than buried: this split also absorbs preformed-d13C
and air-sea-disequilibrium structure that a two-box surface/deep contrast
cannot separate, and the observed surface d13C is Suess-depleted while the
deep is much less so. Treat the percentages as an order, not a partition.


